{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because I want relaxed blues and familiar guitar playing right now.",
    "Hypnotic Eye appeals through the tougher guitar-led rock I enjoyed in People, Hell & Angels, while A Fool To Care and Blue & Lonesome also fit my current blues interest."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Firewatcher's Daughter and Supernova feel less suited to this visit because I am looking for blues guitar rather than a folk-oriented or psychedelic direction.",
    "Sleepwalk's instrumental oldies focus does not match what I want today; an older guitar sound alone is not enough to make it appealing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations sometimes treat broadly related rock and roots records as equally relevant, although their musical direction matters to me.",
    "My interest in thoughtful songwriting seems to carry too much weight for this visit: Standing in the Breach interests me, but it is less immediate than a blues-focused choice."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection from Old Sock to relaxed blues guitar matters especially strongly to me right now.",
    "I rarely choose many records at once, so being interested in an album does not mean I will select it today; several appealing titles lose out to my two strongest choices."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in guitar-led rock and roots music, but only some capture the blues-focused mood driving my choices today."
}"}
